│ patch_name               │ hex_layout_refinement_loop                                                                │
│ patch_description        │ The current hexagonal layout gives sum ≈ 2.36. The main limitation is that the fixed      │
│                          │ lattice positions are not optimal — circles near the walls are too far from them and      │
│                          │ circles near the top row (only 3 circles) waste space. A powerful, still                  │
│                          │ "constructor-style" improvement is to add a deterministic local refinement loop: after    │
│                          │ computing radii, each center is nudged toward the direction that increases its available  │
│                          │ space (away from close neighbors, toward the walls), then radii are re-grown. We keep the │
│                          │ best configuration seen across iterations, guaranteeing we never get worse. This emulates │
│                          │ the "relaxation" step that produces the AlphaEvolve-style packings while remaining fully  │
│                          │ deterministic and feasible (radii are always computed by the safe grow_radii routine).    │
