│ patch_name               │ relax_and_regrow_packing                                                                  │
│ patch_description        │ The current constructor fixes centers on a hex lattice and only grows radii. The leftover │
│                          │ space near walls/corners is wasted because centers never move. I propose adding a         │
│                          │ deterministic relaxation phase: after greedy radius growth, each center is pushed         │
│                          │ slightly away from touching neighbors and toward the interior from walls (Lloyd-style     │
│                          │ repulsion), then radii are re-grown. We keep the best configuration seen across           │
│                          │ iterations. This lets edge circles slide into corners and staggered rows shift to fill    │
│                          │ gaps, typically raising the sum of radii well above a static lattice. The process is      │
│                          │ fully deterministic (fixed iteration count, fixed order), so the constructor remains      │
│                          │ explicit and reproducible.                                                                │
