│ patch_description        │ Instead of concentric rings (which waste corners), this constructor uses a                │
│                          │ hexagonal-lattice-inspired explicit layout: staggered rows of circles filling the square. │
│                          │ Circles are placed in 5 staggered rows (6+5+6+5+4 = 26 positions). Radii are computed by  │
│                          │ solving the exact constraint: each circle's radius is limited by its nearest neighbors    │
│                          │ and walls. We place centers on a staggered grid with a small gradient (slightly larger    │
│                          │ circles at the bottom/top rows), then compute maximal radii via pairwise scaling          │
│                          │ iteration so no overlaps occur and everything is valid. This layered hexagonal pattern is │
│                          │ much closer to the known optimal ~2.6 structure than ring-based placement.                │
