│                          │ instead of a fixed uniform target radius during relaxation, we alternate between (a)      │
│                          │ computing exact max radii via vectorized proportional scaling and (b) pushing overlapping │
│                          │ circles apart proportionally to their current radii — a Lloyd-style relaxation adapted to │
│                          │ the actual radii, letting larger circles dominate. Additionally, several lattice spacings │
│                          │ are tried and the best-sum arrangement is kept, improving robustness of the initial       │
│                          │ layout. Output format (centers, radii, sum_radii) is unchanged.                           │
