│ patch_name               │ multistart_jitter_refinement                                                              │
│ patch_description        │ The current refinement is a single greedy pass that easily gets stuck. Key expert         │
│                          │ insight: for n=26, equal-radius square/hex grids (25 circles at r=0.1 → sum 2.5) already  │
│                          │ beat the current 2.36, and larger sums come from variable radii with corner circles       │
│                          │ exploiting boundary space. I improve the constructor by (1) adding more candidate seed    │
│                          │ layouts including a plain 5×5+1 grid (guaranteed sum ≥ ~2.5 before refinement), (2)       │
│                          │ running a deterministic multi-start refinement: each candidate is jittered with a         │
│                          │ fixed-seed RNG and re-grown, keeping the best, and (3) increasing refinement iterations.  │
│                          │ This gives the growth heuristic many chances to escape local optima and let corner/edge   │
│                          │ circles enlarge, pushing the sum toward the 2.6+ range while keeping feasibility (radii   │
│                          │ only grow under the validated grow_radii routine).                                        │
