│ patch_description        │ The current lattice gives sum 2.37 but leaves wasted space near corners and between       │
│                          │ staggered rows. Instead of a single fixed grow pass, alternate (a) fully vectorized       │
│                          │ radius growth to the true feasibility limit for current centers, and (b) a                │
│                          │ center-relaxation step that pushes each circle away from its most binding constraint      │
│                          │ (wall or neighbor), with a decaying step size plus tiny deterministic jitter. Keeping the │
│                          │ best valid configuration found gives a monotone improvement over the current constructor  │
│                          │ while remaining a short refinement of an explicit layout, pushing the sum toward the      │
│                          │ 2.635 target.                                                                             │
