│ patch_name               │ multi_layout_search_and_contact_relaxation                                                │
│ patch_description        │ Two improvements: (1) Enumerate several lattice topologies (row counts / stagger /        │
│                          │ spacing) and keep the best after relaxation, rather than one fixed layout. (2) After      │
│                          │ picking the best layout, run a "contact relaxation" pass: iteratively move each center to │
│                          │ equalize the gap to its nearest constraints (neighbors and walls), allowing it to grow    │
│                          │ its own radius — this directly maximizes sum_radii at convergence rather than only        │
│                          │ enforcing a uniform target radius. The uniform-radius repulsion tends to leave circles    │
│                          │ with excess slack near walls and between rows; the local gap-equalization pass recovers   │
│                          │ that slack.                                                                               │
