│ patch_name               │ hex_lattice_multicandidate_vectorized                                                     │
│ patch_description        │ Crosses the multi-candidate lattice enumeration from the first program with the hexagonal │
│                          │ lattice relaxation of the second. Enumerates several staggered/square row layouts across  │
│                          │ multiple lattice spacings, relaxes each with a fully vectorized pairwise repulsion        │
│                          │ (instead of the slow O(n^2) Python loops), computes maximum radii with a vectorized       │
│                          │ proportional-scaling loop, and returns the best configuration by total radii. This keeps  │
│                          │ the speed of program 1's vectorization while ensuring the candidate selection and scoring │
│                          │ work correctly (program 1's low score came from evaluating candidates with an effective   │
│                          │ radius that collapsed radii), and improves over program 2's single layout by trying many  │
│                          │ topologies.                                                                               │
