                        Patch Metadata - Gen 22/200 - Novelty: 1/3 - Resample: 1/3 - Patch: 1/3                         
╭──────────────────────────┬───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────╮
│ Field                    │ Value                                                                                     │
├──────────────────────────┼───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤
│ patch_type               │ diff                                                                                      │
│ patch_name               │ greedy_void_filling_after_refine                                                          │
│ patch_description        │ After the refine/growth loop converges, the lattice-based layout still leaves interior    │
│                          │ voids and under-used boundary regions. Grid-sample the square to find the point           │
│                          │ maximizing distance to all circle boundaries and the walls (the largest inscribed void    │
│                          │ radius). If this void radius exceeds ~0.05, insert a new circle there, re-run             │
│                          │ refine_layout on 27 centers so everything re-equilibrates around the newcomer, and then   │
│                          │ drop the smallest circle to return to n=26. This is the interior-space generalization of  │
│                          │ greedy boundary capture: the new circle captures space that the fixed-lattice arrangement │
│                          │ cannot, and re-refinement lets neighboring circles redistribute. Repeat the insertion     │
