│ patch_name               │ greedy_void_filling_refinement                                                            │
│ patch_description        │ The current program regressed from 2.42 to 2.36 because the greedy void-filling +         │
│                          │ re-refinement loop was dropped. Re-add it: after picking the best lattice candidate,      │
│                          │ grid-sample the square to find the largest interior void; if it admits a circle with      │
│                          │ radius > 0.04, append it as a 27th center, re-refine with the existing `refine_layout`    │
│                          │ (which lets SLSQP-like reshuffling of neighbors happen via the push/pull nudge            │
│                          │ heuristic), drop the smallest circle to return to n=26, re-grow, and keep the result if   │
│                          │ the sum improves. Add a helper `find_largest_void` using vectorized grid sampling. This   │
│                          │ exploits interior gaps that the boundary-pulling heuristic leaves unexploited, which      │
│                          │ previously yielded +0.01–0.06 on top of the lattice layout.                               │
