│ patch_type               │ diff                                                                                      │
│ patch_name               │ slsqp_polish_optimizer                                                                    │
│ patch_description        │ The current program's weakness is its crude relaxation heuristic — the "contact_relax"    │
│                          │ step only moves centers based on a single nearest neighbor and the proportional-scaling   │
│                          │ radius assignment does not jointly optimize centers and radii. The gap to 2.635 requires  │
│                          │ a proper joint nonlinear optimization: treat all 26 centers and radii as decision         │
│                          │ variables (78 dims), maximize sum(r) subject to pairwise non-overlap constraints r_i +    │
│                          │ r_j <= d_ij and wall constraints r_i <= min(x_i, y_i, 1-x_i, 1-y_i). SLSQP handles this   │
│                          │ well from a feasible lattice seed. Additionally, since SLSQP may end slightly infeasible, │
│                          │ we add a guaranteed repair step (shrink radii until feasible), then re-run SLSQP a second │
│                          │ "polish" pass from the repaired point so fine-grained contact adjustments can be made.    │
│                          │ This replaces the ad-hoc contact relaxation with a principled optimizer while remaining   │
│                          │ deterministic.                                                                            │
