│ patch_description        │ The current program regressed to 2.10 versus the earlier 2.42 program. The key            │
│                          │ differences: (1) the earlier program generated a diverse pool of seed layouts (multiple   │
│                          │ row-count patterns × stretch factors × jittered variants) rather than a single fixed hex  │
│                          │ core, and (2) it refined positions with a deterministic greedy nudge toward free space,   │
│                          │ keeping only improvements. Layout diversity in the seed pool is what drives the score. I  │
│                          │ restore that framework and enhance it: add corner-filler seed variants (small circles     │
│                          │ tucked into the four corners alongside the hex core, which the current program showed     │
│                          │ helps), add wall-contact variants of the row layouts, and use the monotone Gauss-Seidel   │
│                          │ radius grower with a final greedy position refinement pass. Each candidate gets its radii │
│                          │ grown exactly, positions nudged toward free space, and only improving configurations are  │
│                          │ kept, so validity remains 1.0.                                                            │
