│ patch_name               │ cobyla_refinement_variant                                                                 │
│ patch_description        │ Add a second refinement pass using COBYLA on a penalized objective for each lattice       │
│                          │ candidate, keeping whichever result (SLSQP or COBYLA) gives the higher repaired sum.      │
│                          │ COBYLA's derivative-free, trust-region approach often escapes the local optima where      │
│                          │ SLSQP stalls, and starting it from the SLSQP output (a warm start) lets it explore the    │
│                          │ constraint boundary differently. Every output still goes through `_repair`, so            │
│                          │ feasibility is guaranteed. This is the highest-leverage untested axis within the proven   │
│                          │ framework (refinement method dominates score spread 2.42→2.61), and it adds only modest   │
│                          │ extra runtime.                                                                            │
