│ patch_description        │ The best prior program (gen 4, 2.42) gained most of its value from seed *diversity* (many │
│                          │ hex row layouts plus jittered variants) followed by a simple nudge-and-grow refinement.   │
│                          │ The current program regressed to a single seed with repulsion relaxation (2.37). I        │
│                          │ propose restoring the multi-seed pool from gen 4, but adding two improvements motivated   │
│                          │ by packing geometry:                                                                      │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ 1. **Directional hill climbing on centers**: after the nudge refinement, do a             │
│                          │ coordinate-wise local search — for each circle, test moves along the four axis directions │
│                          │ and away-from-nearest-neighbor, keep any move that increases the total grown radius. This │
│                          │ directly exploits the fact that a circle's radius is min(wall distances, neighbor gaps),  │
│                          │ so moving toward the most binding constraint's slack is a first-order improvement, unlike │
│                          │ the fixed repulsion heuristic.                                                            │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ 2. **Iterative maximal-radii assignment**: use the constraint-propagation                 │
│                          │ `compute_max_radii` (which shrinks only violating circles) inside the refinement loop,    │
│                          │ since it yields a larger (maximal) radius assignment than proportional scaling — every    │
│                          │ refined configuration scores higher.                                                      │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ The search is deterministic (fixed RNG seed), self-contained in numpy, and each candidate │
│                          │ refinement is cheap (vectorized distance matrices), keeping eval time bounded. Seed       │
│                          │ diversity + finer local search should push past 2.42 toward the 2.6 range.                │
