│ patch_name               │ slsqp_polish_restart                                                                      │
│ patch_description        │ The current pipeline runs SLSQP once from a crude lattice seed, repairs (shrinking        │
│                          │ radii), then applies COBYLA to every candidate — costing 51s eval time with no score gain │
│                          │ (both runs at 2.61). The recommended edit implements the "polish pass": after repair,     │
│                          │ restart SLSQP from the feasible repaired (centers, radii). Since this warm start is       │
│                          │ already feasible and near a local optimum with many active tangency constraints, SLSQP    │
│                          │ can make the fine tangency adjustments (growing radii against walls and neighbors) that   │
│                          │ the crude seed cannot reach — the most direct route toward closing the gap to 2.635. We   │
│                          │ apply a second (and third) polish round while it keeps improving. Additionally, we only   │
│                          │ run the expensive COBYLA stage on the single best refined candidate, cutting runtime      │
│                          │ dramatically while keeping the score.                                                     │
