│ patch_type               │ diff                                                                                      │
│ patch_name               │ slsqp_polish_pass                                                                         │
│ patch_description        │ Add an SLSQP-based nonlinear optimization "polish" pass. The current greedy hill-climb    │
│                          │ moves one center at a time with fixed step sizes, so it cannot make coordinated           │
│                          │ simultaneous adjustments that grow the total sum (e.g. shifting whole chains of touching  │
│                          │ circles to open slack). SLSQP can jointly optimize all 52 center coordinates with the sum │
│                          │ of radii as the objective — but since radii must also be variables, we instead use a      │
│                          │ smooth surrogate: maximize sum of "effective radii" computed by a soft-min of the         │
│                          │ pairwise/wall distance constraints. Concretely, we run SLSQP on z = centers (fixed radii  │
│                          │ recomputed by grow_radii is non-smooth), so a cleaner formulation: optimize z =  (78      │
│                          │ vars) with objective -sum(radii), inequality constraints g(z) >= 0 for each wall distance │
│                          │ (r_i - x_i, r_i - (1-x_i), etc.) and each pair (d_ij - r_i - r_j). This directly targets  │
│                          │ the true objective with exact constraints and is smooth. We repair the SLSQP output       │
│                          │ (shrink radii to feasibility via grow_radii logic) and keep it only if it strictly        │
│                          │ improves the valid sum. Applying this only to the best candidate keeps runtime modest     │
│                          │ relative to the current 7.5s budget.                                                      │
│ num_applied              │ 1                                                                                         │
│ api_costs                │ $0.0159                                                                                   │
