│ patch_description        │ Restructure the program into a modular pipeline: (1) seed builders produce diverse        │
│                          │ feasible starting configurations (hex lattice variants, corner-anchored layouts, jittered │
│                          │ copies), (2) each seed is handed to a scipy nonlinear optimizer (`trust-constr` with      │
│                          │ analytic Jacobians, falling back to SLSQP) that jointly optimizes all 52 variables (26    │
│                          │ centers × 2 coords + 26 radii) to maximize the radius sum subject to non-overlap and wall │
│                          │ constraints, (3) a vectorized feasibility repair fixes any tiny violations from the       │
│                          │ solver, and (4) the best candidate is kept. This replaces the greedy grow/nudge heuristic │
│                          │ with true constrained optimization, which per prior evidence dominates the achievable     │
│                          │ score, and modularizes seed generation, refinement, repair, and selection into separate   │
│                          │ functions.                                                                                │
