│ Field                    │ Value                                                                                     │
├──────────────────────────┼───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤
│ patch_type               │ diff                                                                                      │
│ patch_name               │ multi_start_slsqp_and_fast_grow                                                           │
│ patch_description        │ Two targeted improvements: (1) Instead of polishing only the single best heuristic        │
│                          │ candidate with SLSQP, collect all refined candidates, rank them by achieved sum, and run  │
│                          │ the SLSQP continuous polish on the top-5 distinct basins, keeping the overall best.       │
│                          │ Different hex-row count sets lead to genuinely different local optima; polishing several  │
│                          │ of them dramatically increases the chance of landing in a near-global basin (the          │
│                          │ AlphaEvolve n=26 solution is asymmetric, so multiple distinct starting basins matter).    │
│                          │ (2) Vectorize the inner sweep of `grow_radii` with NumPy broadcasting (radii += where     │
│                          │ growth possible via a single vectorized candidate computation). Since `grow_radii` is     │
│                          │ called from inside the 60-iteration refine loop for dozens of candidates, this cuts eval  │
│                          │ time substantially, freeing budget for the extra SLSQP restarts.                          │
│ num_applied              │ 2                                                                                         │
│ api_costs                │ $0.0256                                                                                   │
