│ Field                    │ Value                                                                                     │
├──────────────────────────┼───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤
│ patch_type               │ diff                                                                                      │
│ patch_name               │ expand_jittered_seed_diversity                                                            │
│ patch_description        │ The recommendation targets the identified bottleneck: seed diversity. Currently only      │
│                          │ `cands[0]` receives 4 jittered variants; the other ~8 valid row-set layouts get none, and │
│                          │ `r_init` is fixed at 0.05 for all candidates. Prior generations showed that multi-start   │
│                          │ jittered diversity was the single biggest gain (2.42 → 2.61). I propose: (1) generate 2   │
│                          │ deterministic Gaussian-jittered variants (σ=0.015) per valid layout using a distinct      │
│                          │ per-layout RNG seed, (2) add radius-level diversification by scaling `r_init` by          │
│                          │ 0.9/1.0/1.1 per candidate, and (3) propagate the per-candidate `r_init` through           │
│                          │ `construct_packing` into `_refine` so the radius initialization scale also diversifies.   │
│                          │ This roughly triples the candidate pool cheaply (SLSQP per-candidate cost unchanged),     │
│                          │ greatly increasing the chance that at least one seed basin leads SLSQP past 2.61 toward   │
│                          │ the 2.635 target.                                                                         │
│ num_applied              │ 2                                                                                         │
│ api_costs                │ $0.0199                                                                                   │
