│ Field                    │ Value                                                                                     │
├──────────────────────────┼───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤
│ patch_type               │ diff                                                                                      │
│ patch_name               │ polish_top_candidates                                                                     │
│ patch_description        │ Currently only the single best lattice candidate receives the expensive SLSQP restart     │
│                          │ polish and COBYLA refinement. However, the crude lattice seed sum is a noisy predictor of │
│                          │ post-polish quality — a slightly worse seed can polish to a better local optimum due to   │
│                          │ different tangency structure. This is a well-known phenomenon in circle packing           │
│                          │ optimization: the basin of attraction of the constrained NLP solver is irregular.         │
│                          │ Polishing the top-k candidates (k=3) and keeping the overall best costs modest extra      │
│                          │ runtime (eval_time was ~9.7s with ample headroom) and directly targets the remaining      │
│                          │ ~0.025 gap to 2.635. Additionally, feeding the repaired point back as the warm start for  │
│                          │ the next SLSQP restart inside `_polish` already exists; we also increase rounds slightly  │
│                          │ and make COBYLA's rhobeg smaller (0.005) for finer tangency adjustments.                  │
│ num_applied              │ 3                                                                                         │
